        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Snippet Extraction Process\n├── run() main skill entry \u003c-- 4a\n│   ├── processFiles() validate \u0026 read \u003c-- 4b\n│   │   ├── validate paths through PathValidator \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:1017\n│   │   ├── resolve symlinks \u0026 re-validate \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:1028\n│   │   └── read file content with limits \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:1048\n│   └── extractSnippets() find matches \u003c-- 4c\n│       ├── extractKeywords() from question \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:738\n│       ├── for each file result\n│       │   ├── extractSymbolBody() if symbol_id \u003c-- 4d\n│       │   │   ├── parseSymbolName() from ID \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:554\n│       │   │   ├── detectLanguage() from extension \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:563\n│       │   │   ├── extractGoSymbolBody() for Go files \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:465\n│       │   │   └── extractSymbolBodyHeuristic() fallback \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:523\n│       │   └── findMatchingLines() keywords \u003c-- 4e\n│       │       ├── splitLines() content \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:778\n│       │       ├── check each line for keywords\n│       │       └── groupIntoBlocks() with context \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:807\n│       └── makeInlinePreviews() for output \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:883",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe snippet extraction system solves the **core problem** of finding relevant code blocks when you have a natural language question. Imagine asking \"how does authentication work?\" - you don't want entire files, you want the specific functions, classes, and code blocks that actually implement authentication. This system takes candidate files from search and intelligently extracts only the most relevant snippets, using both **keyword matching** and **symbol-aware extraction** to understand code structure.\n\n## Details\n\nThe process starts with the main entry point [4a] which receives candidate files and a question. First, it validates and reads each file [4b], ensuring paths are safe and content is loaded within size limits. Then the real intelligence begins: it extracts meaningful keywords from your question and finds matching lines in each file [4e].\n\nWhat makes this system smart is its **symbol-aware extraction**. When a symbol_id is provided (like \"auth.go:Login\"), it uses language-specific parsing to extract the complete function or class body [4d]. For Go files, it uses the AST to find exact boundaries [4d], while for other languages it uses heuristic pattern matching based on language syntax rules.\n\nThe system groups matching lines into logical code blocks with surrounding context, then ranks them by relevance to surface the most useful snippets first. Finally, it creates inline previews for immediate display and can persist full snippets as artifacts when the content is too large [4a].\n\nThe result is precise, context-aware code extraction that understands both **what you're asking for** and **how code is structured**."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "title": "Ripgrep Context Expansion",
      "description": "Performs ripgrep searches and expands matches to surrounding code blocks using language-specific heuristics",
      "locations": [
