        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Context Ripgrep Main Flow\n├── run() skill entry point \u003c-- 5a\n│   ├── ripgrep.SearchJSON() execution \u003c-- 5b\n│   │   └── Parse raw matches from JSON \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/main.go:279\n│   ├── Group matches by file \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/main.go:187\n│   └── For each file:\n│       ├── Read file content \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/main.go:136\n│       ├── NewExpander() creation \u003c-- 5c\n│       │   └── Set language \u0026 max lines \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/expander.go:33\n│       └── ExpandMatches() call \u003c-- 5d\n│           └── For each match:\n│               └── findBlockBoundaries() \u003c-- 5e\n│                   ├── Detect language type \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/expander.go:40\n│                   ├── Search upward for symbol \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/expander.go:175\n│                   └── Find block end (brace/indent) \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/expander.go:509\n└── Format blocks as output \u003c-- skills/code_context_ripgrep/main.go:209",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen you search code with ripgrep, you get individual line matches that lack context. A function definition might be on line 15, but the interesting code could be on line 150. The **code/context_ripgrep** skill solves this by expanding ripgrep matches to their surrounding code blocks - functions, methods, classes - giving you **meaningful context** instead of isolated lines.\n\n## Details\n\nThe skill starts by executing ripgrep to find pattern matches [5a][5b]. For each file with matches, it reads the content and creates a language-specific expander [5c]. The expander uses regex patterns to identify code structures - functions, classes, methods - and finds the boundaries of the block containing each match [5d][5e].\n\nFor Go files, it searches upward for `func` or `type` declarations, then uses brace matching to find the block end. For Python, it tracks indentation levels. For JavaScript/TypeScript, it looks for function declarations and arrow functions. The system groups overlapping matches into single blocks to avoid duplication and formats the results with symbol names and line ranges.\n\nThe result is a set of **complete code blocks** rather than scattered line matches, making it much easier to understand the context around your search terms."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps the complete code search pipeline in foxctl, from user-facing skills through retrieval orchestration to final snippet extraction. Key locations include the smart search orchestration [1b], retrieval generation logic [2a], semantic search implementation [3b], snippet extraction process [4c], and ripgrep block expansion [5e].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph SmartSearch[\"Smart Search Pipeline\"]\n        style SmartSearch fill:#fcc2d7\n        1a[\"1a: Smart Search Entry\u003cbr/\u003erun function\"]\n        1b[\"1b: Generate Candidates\u003cbr/\u003ecalls retrieval.Generator\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Invoke Snippet Extract\u003cbr/\u003ecalls code/snippet_extract skill\"]\n        1a --\u003e 1b\n        1a --\u003e 1e\n    end\n\n    subgraph Retrieval[\"Retrieval Orchestration\"]\n        style Retrieval fill:#a5d8ff\n        2a[\"2a: Generate Method\u003cbr/\u003eorchestrates all sources\"]\n        2b[\"2b: Symbol Index Search\u003cbr/\u003esearches indexed symbols\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Semantic Vector Search\u003cbr/\u003eembedding-based search\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Ripgrep Fallback\u003cbr/\u003ekeyword-based fallback\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Merge and Rank\u003cbr/\u003ecombines all sources\"]\n        2a --\u003e 2b\n        2a --\u003e 2c\n        2a --\u003e 2d\n        2b --\u003e 2e\n        2c --\u003e 2e\n        2d --\u003e 2e\n    end\n\n    subgraph SemanticImpl[\"Semantic Search Implementation\"]\n        style SemanticImpl fill:#a5d8ff\n        3a[\"3a: Semantic Search Entry\u003cbr/\u003emain semantic search\"]\n        3b[\"3b: Generate Query Embedding\u003cbr/\u003econverts question to vector\"]\n        3c[\"3c: Hybrid Search Execution\u003cbr/\u003eBM25 + vector search\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Convert to Candidates\u003cbr/\u003etransforms results\"]\n        3a --\u003e 3b\n        3b --\u003e 3c\n        3c --\u003e 3d\n    end\n\n    subgraph SnippetExtraction[\"Snippet Extraction\"]\n        style SnippetExtraction fill:#b2f2bb\n        4a[\"4a: Snippet Extract Entry\u003cbr/\u003erun function\"]\n        4b[\"4b: Process Candidate Files\u003cbr/\u003evalidates and reads files\"]\n        4c[\"4c: Extract Snippets\u003cbr/\u003efinds matching blocks\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Symbol-Aware Extraction\u003cbr/\u003eAST-based for Go\"]\n        4e[\"4e: Keyword Matching\u003cbr/\u003efinds matching lines\"]\n        4a --\u003e 4b\n        4b --\u003e 4c\n        4c --\u003e 4d\n        4c --\u003e 4e\n    end\n\n    subgraph RipgrepSystem[\"Ripgrep Context Expansion\"]\n        style RipgrepSystem fill:#ffec99\n        5a[\"5a: Context Ripgrep Entry\u003cbr/\u003erun function\"]\n        5b[\"5b: Execute Ripgrep Search\u003cbr/\u003eruns ripgrep pattern match\"]\n        5c[\"5c: Create Language Expander\u003cbr/\u003elanguage-specific detector\"]\n        5d[\"5d: Expand to Code Blocks\u003cbr/\u003eexpands matches to blocks\"]\n        5e[\"5e: Find Block Boundaries\u003cbr/\u003edetects function/class boundaries\"]\n        5a --\u003e 5b\n        5a --\u003e 5c\n        5b --\u003e 5d\n        5c --\u003e 5d\n        5d --\u003e 5e\n    end\n\n    1b --\u003e|generates candidates| 2a\n    2c --\u003e|calls semantic search| 3a\n    1e --\u003e|extracts snippets from| 4a\n    2e --\u003e|returns candidates to| 1b\n    3d --\u003e|returns candidates to| 2c"
}